WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.135
-We are back, everybody.

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:04.871
John Cena is here with us
in studio!

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.506
-Seven live audience members.

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:09.775
-From New York City.
Studio 6A at 30 Rock.

00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:12.679
I'm so happy you're here.
Your fans want to hear about it.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.580
I want to hear about
"Fast 9."

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.582
I know -- Yeah, I know.
This is --

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:18.118
We were talking about it,
and you were like,

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:20.787
"Oh, get ready, man. The stunts
on this is just insanity."

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:23.155
-Well, that's the thing.
I think, so "Fast 9,"

00:00:23.155 --> 00:00:25.525
very similar to BTS, they have
this global fanbase.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:27.360
Because they've been making
these movies for 20 years.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.628
-Sure.
-So it's been

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.196
a legacy project, you know?

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.730
And the newest installment --

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:34.133
like, everybody knows "Fast"
is gonna kill it

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.401
when it comes to action.

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:38.271
The thing I love about "Fast 9"

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:42.775
is people are gonna see it
weave that legacy together.

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:44.377
And it's not --

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:47.212
You know, it's not merely
what is "Fast"

00:00:47.212 --> 00:00:49.348
gonna do next for action.

00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:51.817
It is action
on the edge of your seat,

00:00:51.817 --> 00:00:54.520
but story, if you're
a fan of the franchise,

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.589
like, you get questions
answered,

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.291
you get new questions
you develop.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:02.028
Like, it's another foothold
to the narrative,

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.863
which that's the stuff
that I love.

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.798
-Were you nervous
walking onto set?

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:07.333
Because hey all know each other
for years.

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:09.602
-Normally, no.
Normally, it's a job

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:12.138
and movies
are kind of like summer camp

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:13.840
where you meet people
for the first time

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.374
and then you establish
relationships

00:01:15.374 --> 00:01:16.475
and then you move on.

00:01:16.475 --> 00:01:18.578
"Fast" is different
because literally

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.412
it's been 20 years
in the making.

00:01:20.412 --> 00:01:22.148
So walking in the set of "Fast"

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:25.685
was similar to walking into
the WWE locker room.

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:28.187
You have guys --
and men and women

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:30.689
who risk their lives
for a living,

00:01:30.689 --> 00:01:33.559
and have curated this experience
that they're very proud of.

00:01:33.559 --> 00:01:35.294
So when we get a newcomer
to walk in,

00:01:35.294 --> 00:01:38.131
like, you can't help it
but like,

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.100
"Man, I hope this person
works out

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:44.437
because I'm killing myself
for this."

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.039
-It's my new brother-in-law.
-Everybody --

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:48.674
When I'm like -- And I'm
geeked out on "Fast,"

00:01:48.674 --> 00:01:50.910
so I'm looking at like
Dom Toretto,

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.845
I'm looking at him going,
"Oh, my God."

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:54.914
And it's like this,
it's like...

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.782
Dude, it's like the Vin look,
like...

00:01:56.782 --> 00:01:58.951
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:00.619
-And not just him, bro.
Everybody.

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:03.055
Everybody was like, "Yo."
-They know how to play, yeah.

00:02:03.055 --> 00:02:04.791
-"What's up with the new kid?"
And I've never --

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:07.426
Like, I felt just as much
pressure as my first month

00:02:07.426 --> 00:02:08.828
on the road in WWE.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:12.098
But what I love about
the "Fast" family

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:15.568
is that as soon as they see that
you're a fan of the franchise,

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.937
that your intention
is for the family,

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:20.139
bro, they take you in,
and it really is --

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:22.241
Like, they talk so much
about family.

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:24.009
And like, I owe so much to Vin

00:02:24.009 --> 00:02:26.045
for not only allowing me
to be in the movie,

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:28.081
but making me better
as a performer.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:30.049
But it's a family.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.550
It's weird to say.
-You get close.

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:33.986
-It's also the camaraderie
of WWE.

00:02:33.986 --> 00:02:35.889
Like, once you're in,
you're in.

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:37.923
-Yeah, and you help each other.
-And, man, it was awesome.

00:02:37.923 --> 00:02:39.759
I had a blast filming that one.

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:42.028
Not only do you do
crazy stuff, but like --

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:44.229
-We got a picture of some
stunt you were doing.

00:02:44.229 --> 00:02:48.000
They sent us a photo of you,
one scene in the movie.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.236
This is exclusive to our show.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:53.472
This is you like zip lining
over Edinburgh.

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:55.074
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.943
-I kind of took that place over
for a few days.

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:59.178
-Are you good with heights?

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:01.614
-No, no, not at all.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:03.283
So that was the toughest
thing about "Fast,"

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:05.451
is like you gotta do this
crazy [bleep],

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.620
but you have to look like
it doesn't affect you.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:08.687
-Yeah.
-And I --

00:03:08.687 --> 00:03:10.189
Like, if they close up
and HD that,

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:11.791
you would see a puddle
in my pants.

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.225
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.225 --> 00:03:15.495
I done peed myself but I have to
look like it's nothing.

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:17.330
Whoosh! All right, here we go!
-Yeah.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.365
So you'll see in the movie,
I look pretty tough.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.033
But I had already peed myself
a few times.

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.435
-Okay, yeah, I would have
freaked out,

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:25.938
because I went zip lining
with Tariq in Puerto Rico.

00:03:25.938 --> 00:03:29.041
And...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:31.077
-You don't look afraid.
-Here's me and Tariq.

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:32.912
-Yeah, there you go.
-Yeah.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:36.249
And that's my -- that's my...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:37.784
-If it's any consolation,
that's how I felt

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:39.252
on the inside.
-Yeah.

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:41.620
This was my audition
for "Fast 9," they didn't --

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.722
-We're just going to go
in another direction.

00:03:43.722 --> 00:03:45.057
Just gonna go another way.

00:03:45.057 --> 00:03:46.258
Love you. Love you.
-Jimmy, we love you.

00:03:46.258 --> 00:03:47.359
-We're just gonna
go another way.

00:03:47.359 --> 00:03:48.594
-You're my favorite,

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:50.129
we're just gonna go in
a different direction.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:52.998
[ Laughs ] And then
"Suicide Squad."

00:03:52.998 --> 00:03:54.167
-Yep.
-Come on.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.268
-You're playing Peacemaker.

00:03:56.268 --> 00:03:57.837
People are freaking out.
Even --

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.271
There's nothing even
in the trailer,

00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:01.807
just a list of names, and
people are like, "What?!"

00:04:01.807 --> 00:04:03.876
-I think the most important
thing as far as

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:06.845
"The Suicide Squad" is concerned
is the name James Gunn.

00:04:06.845 --> 00:04:09.682
And people know James and his
passion to tell the story,

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:10.983
his passion to weave a narrative

00:04:10.983 --> 00:04:12.618
and develop characters
you care about.

00:04:12.618 --> 00:04:14.654
A perfect template for that
is "Guardians."

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:17.623
As just a general moviegoer
I knew nothing about

00:04:17.623 --> 00:04:19.592
"Guardians," but five minutes
into the movie

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.260
I loved the characters.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:24.230
And that's what he does
so well.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.332
-Are they spinning off
your character already

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:28.100
into like a --
I heard like a show?

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:31.103
-Mm, yes. Noes. Yes. Yes.

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:33.139
-Okay, I was like, wait --

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:34.840
-I mean, this is also,
you know,

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:37.376
you try do the best you can
with every opportunity.

00:04:37.376 --> 00:04:40.079
I really loved "Suicide Squad"
and got along great with James.

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:42.282
I was like, "Hey, man,
we should do this again."

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:43.916
He's like, "Yeah,
we should do this again."

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:46.218
Pretty soon it was like, "Yo,
wanna do a show for HBO Max?"

00:04:46.218 --> 00:04:48.388
I was like, "What? Yes."
-This is fantastic

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:50.088
having an in-studio guest
because I'm getting

00:04:50.088 --> 00:04:51.257
all these exclusives.

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:53.392
You're just, like,
dropping bombs.

00:04:53.392 --> 00:04:54.826
It's fantastic, I love it.

00:04:54.826 --> 00:04:56.128
-So I was down for a bit,

00:04:56.128 --> 00:04:57.663
but now that we're
filming again,

00:04:57.663 --> 00:04:59.131
I'll be -- I'm currently
in production with

00:04:59.131 --> 00:05:01.433
a cool comedy called
"Vacation Friends."

00:05:01.433 --> 00:05:04.203
We just went back to work,
and it's very much like this.

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:05.605
It's very protected
and very safe.

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:07.005
-Safe.
-Telling jokes

00:05:07.005 --> 00:05:08.674
and come here to talk to you
and then go back

00:05:08.674 --> 00:05:11.310
and tell some jokes.
-Yeah, back to work.

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.078
-Can we talk about
"Fast Friends: Elbow Grease"?

00:05:13.078 --> 00:05:14.447
-I would love to.
-Or as I call them,

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:18.083
bow -- "Elbow Grease:
Fast Friends."

00:05:18.083 --> 00:05:19.752
This one, this is
your third one,

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:22.455
and I have the other two.
I read them to my daughters.

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:24.490
I love the messages
in all of these.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:25.925
But this one, there's a new
character,

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:27.260
it's a motorcycle.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.094
-Yes, there's an electric
motorcycle called Chopper,

00:05:29.094 --> 00:05:30.730
and she's very skilled.
-Yes.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:31.897
-She is very skilled.
-She is.

00:05:31.897 --> 00:05:34.233
-That's very important.
So, um,

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:35.935
with the "Elbow Grease" books,

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:37.670
I have a very young audience
at WWE,

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.238
a lot of kids,
lot of families,

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:42.709
and as my in-ring career
is not as --

00:05:42.709 --> 00:05:44.276
it's not as active --
it's not over,

00:05:44.276 --> 00:05:45.811
but it's not as active --

00:05:45.811 --> 00:05:48.247
I wanted to continue
to send messaging

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:50.349
to those younger viewers
because so many times

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:52.117
parents will be like,
"Hey, your 'never give up'

00:05:52.117 --> 00:05:54.620
words have helped
my son or daughter."

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.256
Okay, so I created
a children's book series

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:59.424
that is fun and bright
and colorful

00:05:59.424 --> 00:06:00.993
and about monster trucks.

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:03.095
So first and foremost,
it's a fun read.

00:06:03.095 --> 00:06:04.296
-Yeah.
-And then there's some

00:06:04.296 --> 00:06:07.066
underlying stuff in there
about never giving up.

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:09.735
And because it was a success,
we got to do another book.

00:06:09.735 --> 00:06:11.403
The second book is about
the value of teamwork,

00:06:11.403 --> 00:06:14.540
and this third book
is about being comfortable

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:18.077
in your own skin,
facing insecurities,

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:21.179
jealousy, not judging a book
by its cover, so to speak,

00:06:21.179 --> 00:06:22.514
not being judgmental.

00:06:22.514 --> 00:06:24.283
But only if you choose it.

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:25.918
You can also read the book
and be like,

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:27.954
"It's a cool motorcycle
with cool monster trucks."

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:29.321
-Monster trucks, yeah,
exactly.

00:06:29.321 --> 00:06:30.590
-I think that's really
important

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:32.090
'cause I don't want to hit
anybody over the head

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:33.826
with messaging, I want them
to enjoy the book.

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:35.327
And if they want to take
something away from it,

00:06:35.327 --> 00:06:36.796
they can.
-It's up to you, yeah.

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:39.331
I love it. "Elbow Grease:
Fast Friends"

00:06:39.331 --> 00:06:41.167
is out right now.

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:43.035
John, every time
you've been here, gosh,

00:06:43.035 --> 00:06:46.105
we've done almost every
single sketch together.

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:47.940
-We hit each other with fish
last time.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:49.675
-Last time we -- gosh!
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:51.209
-It's like you're not even
trying anymore.

00:06:51.209 --> 00:06:52.845
Hey, fish slap!

00:06:52.845 --> 00:06:54.780
What's that technical
game about, Jimmy?

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:56.315
-That was a classic.

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:58.050
-What could that ever be about?
-Fish slap was -- yeah.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:59.718
-I don't even have to
explain the rules of fish slap.

00:06:59.718 --> 00:07:01.220
-You don't.
-No.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:04.590
We should do -- by the way,
we should do a sitcom together.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:07.092
Let's stop fooling around.

00:07:07.092 --> 00:07:09.194
-Or should we do like
a buddy cop movie?

00:07:09.194 --> 00:07:11.164
-Oh, yeah.
Like two detectives.

00:07:11.164 --> 00:07:13.299
"Two Dicks."
-Two --

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:14.800
[ Laughter ]

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:17.804
-Okay, so everyone that makes
movies just heard that.

00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:18.905
-Come on!

00:07:18.905 --> 00:07:20.706
-That idea is out
there in the universe.

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:22.675
-Yeah.
-Jimmy Fallon as a dick!

00:07:22.675 --> 00:07:23.742
[ Laughter ]

00:07:23.742 --> 00:07:25.777
John Cena as another dick.

00:07:25.777 --> 00:07:29.281
-Hello, ma'am. Yeah. Yeah.

00:07:29.281 --> 00:07:30.783
"You didn't knock!"

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:32.852
"I can knock and I can ring
the doorbell."

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:33.986
[ Laughter ]
♪♪

00:07:33.986 --> 00:07:35.821
Uh...

00:07:35.821 --> 00:07:39.292
Uh, we have a new game
called...

00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:40.960
[ Laughing ]

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.428
-We have a new game
called Sink the Ship.

00:07:42.428 --> 00:07:44.330
-Toss -- it's called
Toss it Over.

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:45.564
You ready to play
when we come back?

00:07:45.564 --> 00:07:47.366
-Yes, I am.
Of course I will.

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:49.835
[ Laughter ]

00:07:49.835 --> 00:07:51.570
-Not just the name of the game.

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:54.073
John and I are doing something
fun after the break.

00:07:54.073 --> 00:07:55.241
Stick around.

